atalog Law. Lore: Two of Choice prints no bonus and is a pick of two from the Lore rows open to Rifts. Pilot: except Robot Elite and military vehicles is read as the twelve Robot Combat Elite rows and the five Military: pilot rows. Horsemanship is its own catalog category; General and Exotic Animals are offered at the Pilot +10% because Rifts files horsemanship under Pilot, which is a reading. Cowboy: None and Military: None are honoured by leaving those categories out, so Horsemanship: Cowboy is not offered. Hand to Hand: Expert costs three related skills, costs expert 3. || MONEY: 1D6x$1000 in cash/dollars or Universal Credits (the text layer prints lD6x$1000) is starting_money; the book sets the Australian dollar equal to the credit. The 2D6x$1000 in saleable or tradeable stock is goods, not coin, and is in GM Notes, as is An NPC will have twice as much. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: a pair of scissors, a wristwatch, a mini-pocket fan, a suitcase, satchel or briefcase with 10 M.D.C., one suit of excellent quality, personal items, the give-away items and the modest vehicle (typically a jeep, pickup truck or hover car) have no row or are a GM choice and are in GM Notes. One weapon for each W.P. is stored as two generic weapon rows for the two O.C.C. W.P.s. || NOT STORED: the Supply & Demand list the entry points to (printed 70, under the City Trader) is setting text and is summarised in GM Notes; NPC Merchants have 2-8 assistants."
